{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416520-spheres-only-able-to-make-wonders","id":1416520,"title":"Spheres only able to make Wonders","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-02T13:20:27-07:00","id":1416520,"title":"Spheres only able to make Wonders","content":"So thinking about an option brought up in Mage the Podcast that I completely forgot but I always liked, what about the optional rule for half priced spheres that only allow for making Wonders, this can be especially useful for representing Technocrats, Virtual Adepts, Etherites and Solificati. So many technocrats could learn the Wonder only version of Artifacts and rely off of Devices and technological wonders while occasionally say learning the full version of the mind sphere to represent Social Engineering. Anyone use this option?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T17:10:36-07:00","id":1416781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416520-spheres-only-able-to-make-wonders#post1416520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So thinking about an option brought up in Mage the Podcast that I completely forgot but I always liked, what about the optional rule for half priced spheres that only allow for making Wonders, this can be especially useful for representing Technocrats, Virtual Adepts, Etherites and Solificati. So many technocrats could learn the Wonder only version of Artifacts and rely off of Devices and technological wonders while occasionally say learning the full version of the mind sphere to represent Social Engineering. Anyone use this option?</div> </div> </div> </div>The learning of the mind sphere for social engineering isn't Technically necessary, as a &quot;Wonder&quot; doesn't technically need to be a physical object in the material world. You could instead make a &quot;Social Technique&quot; wonder using an idea as the object and use it's effect on those that practice the idea in proximity of the person holding the &quot;original&quot; in their head.<br /> <br /> Problems with this arise from the fact that there'll only be one effect per wonder unlike fast-casting and there's also only one wonder, so the effect can't be spread like a virus. &quot;Loosing&quot; the wonder becomes a problem because it's not a material object and can thus be nabbed by astral spirits, mind magic or loosing your train of thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T19:14:25-07:00","id":1416787,"title":"","content":"Probably a mage that has the Spheres to craft a psychological Wonder it's going to make so it's &quot;rooted&quot; into the depths of the mind of the user.As to prevent it from vanishing (with all the Prime invested) by merely loosing the train of tougth, or forgetting. Albeit steal by magick would still be possible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T20:52:02-07:00","id":1417247,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that there are rules already for such Virtual Wonders. They're not as stable as Wonders that use material foundations; but they're still a lot more permanent than simply working a normal Effect. <br /> <br /> The catch with Wonder Spheres is that any Effect you work must first go through the Wonder creation process \u2014 which is long, arduous, and in need of large supplies of Quintessence. And that's <i>before</i> you get into the additional costs for the likes of Talismans and Grimoires. That's why you're getting the half-cost discount, and dealing in Virtual Wonders doesn't change that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T21:03:02-07:00","id":1417252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416520-spheres-only-able-to-make-wonders?p=1417247#post1417247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that there are rules already for such Virtual Wonders. They're not as stable as Wonders that use material foundations; but they're still a lot more permanent than simply working a normal Effect.<br /> <br /> The catch with Wonder Spheres is that any Effect you work must first go through the Wonder creation process \u2014 which is long, arduous, and in need of large supplies of Quintessence. And that's <i>before</i> you get into the additional costs for the likes of Talismans and Grimoires. That's why you're getting the half-cost discount, and dealing in Virtual Wonders doesn't change that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You would be using already built wonders for effects. It would be like Reed Richards or Tony Stark Method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T21:38:13-07:00","id":1417259,"title":"","content":"You don't need Wonder Spheres for that; you just need the Wonders. The only thing Wonder Spheres are good for is determining what sorts of Effects you can put into a Wonder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T21:51:41-07:00","id":1417260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416520-spheres-only-able-to-make-wonders?p=1417259#post1417259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need Wonder Spheres for that; you just need the Wonders. The only thing Wonder Spheres are good for is determining what sorts of Effects you can put into a Wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I know, I'm saying it better represents the majority of Techies who literally aren't aware they are supernatural beings, they think they are just brilliant humans. They would rely on using Wonders, not just the ones they built. Its a limitation that seems interesting and appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T05:35:04-07:00","id":1417313,"title":"","content":"Though that does leave out the old technocrat trick of analysis / technobabble.<br /> <br /> Where you basically do a sherlock holmes style analysis of the situation and predict an outcome, that then becomes a spell that brings about that outcome.<br /> <br /> Or the one where you inform someone of potential side effects of chemicals they've consumed in junk food, and it's basically a life curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T09:15:13-07:00","id":1417332,"title":"","content":"Agreed, the Syndicate, in particular, is big on working Effects that could be channeled through Wonders, but generally aren't. In particular, the Art of Desire frequently uses Abilities and/or personnel as Instruments; but there are also a number of NWO Procedures and Adjustments that tend not to be turned into Wonders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T22:36:26-07:00","id":1417414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416520-spheres-only-able-to-make-wonders?p=1417332#post1417332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed, the Syndicate, in particular, is big on working Effects that could be channeled through Wonders, but generally aren't. In particular, the Art of Desire frequently uses Abilities and/or personnel as Instruments; but there are also a number of NWO Procedures and Adjustments that tend not to be turned into Wonders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always envisioned playing a syndicate mage in their element is like playing a crossbreed between the sims and civilization. They're forte being careful planning and placement of funds to work rituals that progress over the course of Years with the ultimate goal of building near-permanent ongoing effects or wonder-structures that effect entire nations. On the flip side, their paradox backlashes are the worst, sinking anything from small companies to entire nations in so much debt and poverty that it curses generations of humanity with it's after-effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T16:43:36-07:00","id":1417496,"title":"","content":"I think that those big Effects could be duplicated with Wonder Spheres by cranking Abstract Wonders up to eleven. Such a &quot;social scientist&quot; agent would craft whole bureucratic constructs, protocols and financial structures that would hold Effects for those that know how to manipulate them.<br /> <br /> What would suffer it's the improvization in the moment. The capability to crash a deal with anybody with subtle Mind manipulation, the supernatural intimidation, the capability to &quot;read&quot; any situation...etc.<br /> <br /> I think it's better for Technocrats to have <i>both </i>options. They will still use Wonders most of the time, because Wonders (both abstract and concrete) tend to be more potent than rotes - if you have the kind of &quot;endless&quot; resources to mass produce them.<br /> <br /> But it's cumbersome to try and have a Wonder for every spur on the moment situation, and human Agents being able to improvize it's very much on character (NWO or Syndicate agents, that often have to be in the field with little backup, being good examples) - if improvisation wasn't possible or desirable you're much better cutting with the intermediary, and just sending sentient wonders with all the rigth Procedures to do the job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-09-2020, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T14:12:49-07:00","id":1418584,"title":"","content":"IIRC one of the original MtA supplements had rules for 'alchemy' that wasn't a sorcerer path, that would be similar. Although what is being described is more like a more flexible version of the Enchantment hedge path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}